[801-UPD-0044](801-UPD-0044-a-trial-the-kernel-stopped-names-its-fault-in-the-fallback.done) (round 156 found it), [000-KRN-0210](../issues-done/000-KRN-0210-the-updater-group-ran-past-its-limit-once.done) (a read the new boot's prompt answered, another way a line was lost).

## Resolution

Done (2026-11-20). Landed in round 158 (`main` `7a1e938a6b`), with the gate green on both architectures. Its `x86: the updater and an update through the link` (x32-2, 1398 s) and `aarch64: the updater and the modes` (acc-1, 1167 s) ran `trial_confirmed` through `interleaved`.

No kernel change. The UART is shared with the shell by design (see the Problem), so a line the shell's bytes cut is found, not prevented.
